        },
        "accordion_mDTgQ3": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "icon_width": 25,
            "icon_position": "inline-left",
            "heading": "How do I check my tire size?",
            "type_style": "font-heading",
            "heading_size": 120,
            "text": "<p>Look at the <strong>sidewall of your tire</strong> (the outer wall of the tire). You’ll see a series of numbers and letters that look something like this:</p><p><strong>Example:</strong> 225/45R17</p><ul><li><strong>225</strong> = Tire width (in millimeters)<br/></li><li><strong>45</strong> = Tire profile / sidewall height<br/></li><li><strong>R17</strong> = Wheel size (rim diameter in inches)<br/></li></ul><p>👉 The <strong>full tire size is this entire number sequence</strong> printed on the tire.</p><p><strong>Tire Tips:</strong><br/><br/>You can also find your tire size:</p><ul><li>Inside the <strong>driver’s door jamb sticker</strong><br/></li><li>In your <strong>owner’s manual</strong></li></ul>",
            "text_size": 75,
            "tabs_bg_color": "",
            "line_thickness": "normal",
            "spacing_bottom": 0
          }
        },
        "accordion_ptbHFW": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "icon_width": 25,
            "icon_position": "inline-left",
            "heading": "What is your warranty policy?",
            "type_style": "font-heading",
            "heading_size": 120,
            "text": "<h4><strong>Premier Tire – Limited Product & Installation Warranty</strong></h4><p>This Limited Warranty outlines the coverage and conditions applicable to tires, wheels, and related services purchased from <strong>Premier Tire</strong>.</p><p>Premier Tire acts solely as a <strong>retailer and installer</strong> of products manufactured by third parties. All warranties are limited and subject to manufacturer approval where applicable.</p><h4><strong>1. Tire Limited Warranty</strong></h4><p>All tires sold by Premier Tire carry a <strong>two (2) year limited manufacturer defect warranty</strong> covering defects in materials or workmanship under normal driving conditions.</p><p>Select manufacturers including <strong>Continental, Falken, General Tire, and Nexen</strong> may include <strong>Road Hazard Protection</strong>, where applicable.</p><p>All tire warranty coverage is:</p><ul><li><strong>Prorated based on tread wear and time in service</strong><br/></li><li>Subject to manufacturer inspection and approval<br/></li><li>Limited to repair, replacement, or prorated credit only<br/></li></ul><p>Premier Tire does not provide independent tire warranties beyond proper installation at the time of service.</p><h4>Tire Warranty Exclusions</h4><p>Warranty coverage does not apply to:</p><ul><li>Road impacts, potholes, or debris (unless approved under manufacturer road hazard programs)<br/></li><li>Improper inflation, alignment, suspension, or mechanical vehicle issues<br/></li><li>Irregular wear<br/></li><li>Motorsports, commercial, or abnormal use<br/></li><li>Damage occurring after installation<br/></li></ul><h4><strong>2. Wheel Structural Warranty</strong></h4><p>All wheels include a <strong>one (1) year limited manufacturer defect warranty</strong> covering structural manufacturing defects only.</p><p>Structural warranty applies strictly to manufacturing faults and <strong>does not include cosmetic or finish-related conditions</strong>.</p><h4><strong>3. Wheel Finish & Cosmetic Protection Limitations (IMPORTANT)</strong></h4><p>Wheel finishes are considered <strong>wear-and-environmental-sensitive surfaces</strong> and are <strong>not guaranteed against environmental exposure</strong>.</p><p>The following conditions are <strong>expressly excluded from warranty coverage</strong>:</p><ul><li>Corrosion, oxidation, or finish deterioration<br/></li><li>Damage caused by road salt, calcium, brine, or winter chemicals<br/></li><li>Brake dust accumulation or heat exposure<br/></li><li>Automatic or touchless car washes<br/></li><li>Acidic or alkaline cleaning agents<br/></li><li>Pressure washing or improper cleaning methods<br/></li><li>Stone chips, curb damage, scratches, or road debris<br/></li><li>Water spotting or staining<br/></li><li>Chrome peeling, clear coat lifting, or discoloration occurring after installation<br/></li><li>Normal aging or environmental wear<br/></li></ul><h4>Winter Usage Limitation</h4><p>Any wheel <strong>not specifically designated by the manufacturer as winter-approved</strong> will have <strong>all finish-related warranty coverage voided</strong> if used in winter driving conditions.</p><h4><strong>4. Storage Requirement (Off-Season Wheels)</strong></h4><p>To maintain eligibility for any finish-related consideration, wheels must be stored in a <strong>clean, dry, climate-controlled indoor environment</strong> when not in use.</p><p>Storage in garages subject to moisture, outdoor sheds, or uncontrolled environments may result in corrosion and is <strong>not covered under warranty</strong>.</p><h4><strong>5. Custom, Forged & Special-Order Wheels</strong></h4><p>All <strong>custom-built, forged, machined, or special-order wheels</strong> are <strong>final sale</strong> once production has begun.</p><p>Due to the custom manufacturing process:</p><ul><li>Minor variations in finish, machining marks, color tone, or texture are considered normal.<br/></li><li>Fitment approved or requested by the customer becomes the customer’s responsibility.<br/></li><li>Custom orders cannot be cancelled, returned, or exchanged.<br/></li></ul><p>Warranty applies only to verified manufacturing structural defects.</p><h4><strong>6. Installation & Torque Responsibility</strong></h4><p>Premier Tire follows industry-standard installation and torque procedures at the time of service.</p><p>Customers acknowledge and agree that:</p><ul><li>Wheel fasteners must be <strong>re-torqued after 50–100 km of driving</strong>.<br/></li><li>Failure to re-torque may result in loosening caused by normal vehicle operation.<br/></li><li>Premier Tire is not responsible for issues arising after the vehicle leaves the premises.<br/></li></ul><p>Premier Tire assumes no liability for:</p><ul><li>Road conditions<br/></li><li>Driver operation<br/></li><li>Third-party servicing<br/></li><li>Subsequent mechanical or vehicle-related issues.<br/></li></ul><h4><strong>7. No Performance or Damage Guarantee</strong></h4><p>Wheels and tires are exposed to unpredictable road conditions. Premier Tire does <strong>not guarantee protection against bending, cracking, vibration, or cosmetic damage</strong> caused by potholes, impacts, or driving hazards.</p><h4><strong>8. Warranty Claim Requirements</strong></h4><p>All claims must:</p><ul><li>Include original proof of purchase<br/></li><li>Be inspected by Premier Tire<br/></li><li>Receive manufacturer authorization where applicable<br/></li></ul><p>Warranty resolution may include repair, replacement, or prorated credit at manufacturer discretion only.</p><h4><strong>9. Limitation of Liability</strong></h4><p>Premier Tire shall not be liable for any indirect or consequential damages including but not limited to:</p><ul><li>Vehicle damage<br/></li><li>Loss of vehicle use<br/></li><li>Rental vehicles<br/></li><li>Towing expenses<br/></li><li>Loss of income<br/></li><li>Personal inconvenience<br/></li></ul><p>Maximum liability, if any, shall not exceed the original purchase price of the product.</p>",
            "text_size": 75,
            "tabs_bg_color": "",
            "line_thickness": "normal",
            "spacing_bottom": 0
          }
        },
